  "id": "self-effacement",
  "term": "self-effacement",
  "definition": "Self-effacement is the effort to turn attention away from oneself and one’s own troubles, and instead live by higher aims, useful work, and less self-centred feeling. In this historical source, it is presented as the opposite of self-consciousness, self-distrust, and selfish preoccupation.",
